Project Overview

Online examinations require strict monitoring to ensure fairness and prevent malpractice. This project implements a rule-based validation system using a Decision Tree approach to check whether a student’s online exam attempt is valid or violates any rules.

The system evaluates multiple conditions such as login status, exam time validity, camera status, tab switching, and multiple logins before allowing or rejecting exam submission.

🎯 Objectives

To validate online exam rules automatically

To detect rule violations in real time

To allow or reject exam submission based on predefined conditions

To demonstrate decision tree logic using C++

🌳 Decision Tree Concept

A Decision Tree is a flow of conditions where each node represents a rule and each branch represents a YES/NO decision.
Based on student actions, the system navigates through the tree and reaches a final decision.

🧩 Rules Considered

Student must be logged in

Exam must be within allowed time

Camera must be ON

Tab switching should not occur

Multiple logins are not allowed

